Overview
The goal of this project is to analyze patterns in public safety and community service in Chicago using tabular data from the 
City of Chicago Open Data Portal. We will explore temporal and categorical trends in crime reports and 311 service requests to
understand relationships between incident types, request types, and patterns over time.

Our approach is to perform data cleaning, feature engineering, exploratory analysis, and correlation analysis. We aim to identify: 
which types of crime and service requests are most common, whether certain request types correlate with specific crime types, and
how these trends change over time (by day, month, or year). Visualizations such as line charts, bar charts, and heatmaps will 
communicate temporal and categorical patterns.

