Research/Business Questions
1. Are there observable correlations between specific types of crime and specific 311 service requests?
2. How do crime incidents and service requests vary over time (daily, monthly, yearly trends)?

Datasets
1. Chicago Crime Data – Tabular dataset of reported crimes (from 2001 to present) including crime type, date/time, and location 
information. Location will not be analyzed spatially; only temporal and categorical attributes will be used.
Source: City of Chicago Crime Data

2. Chicago 311 Service Requests – Tabular dataset of non-emergency service requests, including request type and date/time. Only
categorical and temporal attributes will be analyzed.
Source: City of Chicago 311 Service Requests

Integration: Both datasets include date/time fields, allowing temporal aggregation and correlation analysis. Common categorical 
fields (e.g., request type vs crime type) can be used for comparative analysis.

Kaggle Clause: All datasets are sourced directly from the City of Chicago Open Data Portal, which ensures official provenance, 
clear licensing, and reproducibility. No Kaggle datasets are used.

