Constraints
Data completeness: Crime and 311 data only reflect reported incidents; unreported events are not included.

Temporal resolution: Time stamps may have inconsistencies or missing values.

Data volume: Large datasets may require sampling or efficient processing strategies.

Categorical ambiguity: Some categories may overlap or be inconsistently labeled across datasets.

Gaps
Need to define which crime types and 311 request types are most relevant to analyze correlations.

Decisions on the appropriate temporal aggregation (daily, weekly, monthly) for meaningful analysis.

Consideration of normalization or scaling when comparing counts across datasets.
